## Reading `summary.json`
For `logistic_regression`, `knn` and `difference_lr_minus_knn` (paired, LR minus kNN, per split):
`mean` over the 50 outer folds and three 95% intervals:
- `corrected`: **primary**. Corrected resampled t interval (Nadeau & Bengio 2003; Bouckaert & Frank 2004):
  mean ± t(0.975, 49) · s · sqrt(1/50 + 30/120), where s is the SD of the 50 fold values. Unlike a plain t interval it
  allows for the training-set overlap across folds and repetitions. The interval is an approximation.
- `naive`: t over the 50 folds treated as independent (df 49). It is anti-conservative and shown only for comparison.
- `repeat`: t over the 10 repetition means (df 9).
Bounds are as computed. They are not clipped to [0, 1].

## Protocol (plan.md §2 of story-repo, as run)
Data: OpenML 61, md5 `ad484452702105cbf3d30f8deaba39a9`, 150 × 4, 3 classes × 50. Outer: `RepeatedStratifiedKFold(5, 10,
random_state=20261017)`. Both methods are scored on the same 50 splits. Standardisation is fitted on the training part inside the
pipeline. LR: multinomial (checked: `predict_proba` equals the softmax of the decision function), lbfgs, L2, C=1, max_iter=10000,
not tuned. kNN: Euclidean, uniform weights. k ∈ {1,3,…,31} is chosen by shuffled stratified 5-fold inner CV on the outer
training set (seed 20261017+1+fold index). Ties go to the smallest k. The model is then refit on the outer training set.
Single-threaded BLAS. Environment: Python 3.11.2 and `code/requirements.txt`, the same on both machines.

Note on the k grid: a first run, made before the plan was read, used k ∈ {1,…,30}. The primary analysis follows the
plan's pre-specified odd grid. The first grid is kept as the robustness variant `k_grid_all_1_30`.

## Findings (numbers from `local/summary.json`, `reproducibility.json`, `robustness.json`)
- Q1: LR mean accuracy 0.9540, 95% corrected interval [0.9156, 0.9924]. kNN 0.9447, [0.8967, 0.9927].
- Q2: paired difference LR − kNN +0.0093, 95% corrected interval [−0.0214, +0.0400] (p = 0.54). No difference is resolved.
  LR is better in 13 splits, kNN in 5, and 32 are tied. The selected k ranges from 1 to 17 (median 7) and never reaches the grid edge 31.
- Q3: Ibex job 53909302 ran on node `cn511-08` (partition `batch`, COMPLETED, 13 s). Its results are **identical** to the local
  `local-compute` run under the element-wise criterion: folds, all 1500 predictions and every summary float are equal. This
  holds across different CPUs (local Intel Xeon Gold 6230, Ibex AMD EPYC 9655). Both runs used the same OpenBLAS 0.3.30/0.3.31
  SkylakeX kernels, single-threaded.
- Robustness: under every variant the corrected interval for the difference contains 0. The difference ranges from −0.0007
  (outer seed 1) to +0.0113 (LR with tuned C). Without standardisation both methods score higher (LR 0.9633, kNN 0.9587).
